// GTK3's C API, imported directly rather than through a third-party Swift
// binding. The reason is maintenance risk: a binding that breaks against a new
// Swift release leaves the whole front-end unbuildable, whereas GTK's C API has
// been stable for over a decade and Swift's C importer handles it unaided.
//
// `[system]` suppresses the warnings GTK's own headers produce; they are not
// ours to fix and would otherwise bury real diagnostics.
//
// No `link` directive: the linker flags come from pkg-config via the
// `pkgConfig:` argument on the systemLibrary target in Package.swift, which
// also keeps the include paths correct across distributions.
module CGtk3 [system] {
    header "shim.h"
    export *
}
